    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "AJ3sw",
      "x": -420,
      "y": 4000,
      "name": "Note — Donut Chart (Chassis)",
      "width": 420,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Donut Chart / Chassis — ported 2026-08-25 from Bryan's chart-chassis POC (\"PieChart, donut variant\").\n\nGeometry\n• Ring 288px, inner radius 0.60 (86/144). Slices start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise.\n• The plot box is 312px, not 288 — the extra 12px on each side is room for the 8px hover explode.\n\nPalette\n• Sequential, not categorical: chart-sequential/seq-700 → seq-300, largest slice to smallest. Bryan's #0d6ad3→#9fc9f9 ramp lands on those five steps within a few units, and the ramp inverts itself in dark mode.\n• The center total never swaps on hover — it recomputes only when a series is toggled off.\n\nStates\n• Default — all series on, every slice at full strength.\n• Hover — focused slice explodes 8px along its centroid; the others drop to 42% opacity; tooltip and legend row-hover appear. Bryan's dim tone is the colour mixed 42% over the surface, so opacity reproduces it exactly.\n• Series Off — the toggled series leaves the ring, the remaining angles and the center total recompute (95 here), and its legend row stays at 35%.\n• Static render (print/PDF) is pixel-identical to Default, so it has no component of its own.\n\nNot reproduced\n• Bryan's 9% \"hot\" lift on the focused slice. In tokens that means borrowing the next ramp step, which is the neighbouring slice's own colour. Explode plus full-vs-dim carries the emphasis instead.\n\nChassis atoms\n• Chart Legend Row — Default / Hover / Off / Focus. Hemlock's InteractiveLegend was not reused: it is a dot-marker list with no row hit-target, while Bryan's row is a 30px button with a rounded swatch, a right-aligned value and a row-hover background.\n• Chart Tooltip / Title Value — name + value(percent), the donut's two-line form.\n• Chart Error Block — the fail-loudly block, shared by every chassis chart."
    }
  ],
  "imports": {
    "T": "../../design-system/in-progress/hemlock-library.lib.pen"
  },
  "fileToken": "c5236207-ea99-4e80-9263-53eca5fd0a16"
